WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.709
Even the most ardent of horror enthusiasts
sometimes have to draw the line.

00:00:03.709 --> 00:00:07.910
In an age in which advancing effects technology
has made it possible to depict incredibly

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:11.829
realistic gross-outs, there's still a limit
to the amount of guts and gore audiences will

00:00:11.829 --> 00:00:14.929
watch before they throw in the popcorn and
give up.

00:00:14.929 --> 00:00:18.010
Here are some horror movies that audiences
walked out of.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:19.929
The Devil's Rejects

00:00:19.929 --> 00:00:24.720
Rob Zombie's sophomore fright feature, a sequel
to 2003's The House of 1000 Corpses, relied

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.080
on the same dark imagery and violence that
made its predecessor so utterly disturbing.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.850
By turning the notch down just a touch on
the slash-and-shock factor in favor of some

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:36.820
more emotionally upsetting moments with The
Devil's Rejects, Zombie earned praise from

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:40.620
a greater number of critics—but still had
some moviegoers hitting the door long before

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.620
the credits rolled.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.699
"I'm gonna have to be taking your car today.

00:00:43.699 --> 00:00:48.340
See I have some top secret clown business
that supersedes any plans that you might have

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:49.899
for this here vehicle."

00:00:49.899 --> 00:00:51.940
Evil Dead

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:56.109
The 1981 version of The Evil Dead was troubling
enough, but the 2013 remake of the creepy

00:00:56.109 --> 00:01:00.379
cult favorite showed off some true next-level
savagery, including a moment of possessed

00:01:00.379 --> 00:01:05.140
self-mutilation of a girl's face and a lot
of vomit spewing, among other debauchery.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:08.310
"Never underestimate the power of puke."

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:12.920
Early viewers at the year's South-by-Southwest
Festival in Austin, Texas got an unexpected

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:17.340
live soundtrack addition: the sounds of many
feet carrying their owners away from the ultra-graphic

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:18.340
brutality.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:21.729
According to Bruce Campbell, who starred in
the original series and served as producer

00:01:21.729 --> 00:01:24.820
on the remake, all the walkouts were considered
a win for the team.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:31.090
He told Hollywood.com: "That's the sign of
a good horror movie."

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:34.310
"Groovy."

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:35.970
The Witch

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:40.560
Critics might have been crazy about this slow-building
period pic about a 17th Century family tormented

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:45.330
by evil, but some audiences didn't quite appreciate
the drawn-out nature of the narrative, which

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:49.790
depended less on jump scares than creepy atmosphere
and a more traditional—and, for some, flat-out

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:50.869
dull—slow-building story.

00:01:50.869 --> 00:01:55.079
Instead of being sent running by the gore,
this time it was the bore factor that drove

00:01:55.079 --> 00:01:56.140
audiences to the exits.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:00.450
"So what you're telling me is to be bored,
and then bored, and finally bored again but

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:02.060
this time for the rest of my life."

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.689
The Witch’s greatest magic trick?

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:09.500
The incredible disappearing audience.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.540
Raw

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:16.320
Some Cannes filmgoers got much more than their
eyes — or stomachs — could handle in 2016,

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.920
when Julia Ducournau's Raw presented them
with the story of a young vegetarian woman

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:23.970
who was hazed into eating raw meat during
school—an act of bullying that awakened

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:27.930
a dormant flesh fetish that was sickening
enough to send audiences rushing for the exit

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:28.930
signs.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:32.561
Whether Raw fits within the usual buffet of
slashers or not, it certainly left a taste

00:02:32.561 --> 00:02:34.830
in everyone's mouth afterward.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:37.150
The Texas Chain Saw Massacre

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:42.230
When the world first met Leatherface in Tobe
Hooper's 1974 slaughterfest, the brazen butchery

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:44.700
was too gruesome for some audience members
to take.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:48.400
The film, in which the power tool-wielding
weirdo trapped and decimated an entire group

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.710
of young friends in ghastly ways, was even
banned in several countries and was originally

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.960
rated X for its grisly violence.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:58.650
One of the scenes that got to audiences most
frequently was the moment when a girl named

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:02.560
Pam was strung up on a meathook and made to
watch as her friend was sliced and diced by

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:03.920
Leatherface's trusty title weapon.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:06.450
You’ll never look at meat the same way again.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:10.620
"Mmm… this is a tasty burger!"

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.610
Ôdishon (Audition)

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:17.690
When this 1999 Japanese torture thriller debuted
at the Rotterdam Film Festival, it won director

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:22.130
Takashi Miike some of the festival's most
prestigious prizes and impressed and inspired

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:26.100
fellow horror auteurs like Eli Roth, John
Landis, and Rob Zombie.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:29.850
The movie's hyper-realistic violence was too
difficult to endure for some audience members,

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:33.200
though, and one woman was even quoted to scream
at the director, "You're evil!"

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.230
during the screening.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:38.090
It wasn't just the eye-gouging and piano wire
foot amputations that made the pic such a

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:42.540
squirmy event—it was also the fact that
the tone took such a drastic turn for the

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:46.410
worse in its third act, after the main character
discovered that the woman he auditioned—hence,

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:51.200
the title—to be his new wife had a twisted
history of inflicting pain on people, up to

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:54.350
and including making a prisoner eat her own
barf.

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:56.440
Thanks, Japan!

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:58.540
"No god!

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:00.590
No god please no!

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:02.170
Please no!"

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:03.170
The Human Centipede

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:07.670
There was enough of an audience interest in
the sick experimentation on display in Tom

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:13.040
Six's The Human Centipede to justify two sequels,
an episode of South Park, and a Key and Peele

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:16.570
sketch, in which former members of a human
centipede all run into each other at a restaurant.

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:17.570
"Hey!

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:18.570
Back-man, back-man!"

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:19.970
"Don't call me that!"

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:23.200
But some who braved the theaters to witness
what happens when a surgeon stitches together

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:27.070
three living humans' digestive systems together
couldn't bear to stick around and see what

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:28.250
came out at the end.

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:32.260
The so-called "First Sequence" was largely
inspired by the notoriously diabolical work

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:37.050
of Josef Mengele at the Auschwitz concentration
camp during World War II, but the director

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:40.830
also said he came up with his sinister plot
after watching the news.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:45.800
"It was a really nasty-looking child molester.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.410
And suddenly I made this joke.

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:52.320
I said they should stitch his mouth to the
ass of a very fat truck driver as a punishment.

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:55.780
And everybody says, 'aww that's such a horrible
idea.'"

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:58.540
No offense, Tom, but next time listen to your
friends...

00:04:58.540 --> 00:04:59.540
Thanks for watching!

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:02.520
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:05.349
And leave us a comment to let us know which
horror movie made you want to walk out...

